+# ADB diagnostics
+
+Build the optional interface with:
+
+~~~sh
+./gradlew :app:assembleRelease -Pduckdetector.adbDiagnostics=true
+~~~
+
+The APK has the version suffix "-adb". It keeps the existing Release R8 and resource
+shrinking configuration. This does not enable JDWP or change native probe thresholds.
+The property defaults to false; ordinary builds do not declare the provider.
+
+Install the APK using the same signing identity as the app being updated, open Duck,
+and complete its usual startup choices. The interface observes those existing sessions.
+It does not start a parallel SDK scanner, grant consent, change root settings, or run
+probes as the ADB shell UID. A disconnected app reports NOT_READY.
+
+## Commands
+
+An already authorized USB or wireless ADB connection is sufficient. No root or TCP
+server is needed. If more than one device is connected, pass "--serial SERIAL"
+before the command.
+
+~~~sh
+python tools/duck-debug.py status
+python tools/duck-debug.py watch --detector selinux --details
+python tools/duck-debug.py scan selinux
+python tools/duck-debug.py report selinux --output selinux-report.txt
+~~~
+
+Use the detector IDs returned by status; the examples assume the catalog ID "selinux".
+Run watch and scan from separate terminals. "scan all" queues all current detector
+sessions. A scan is rejected as BUSY while any detector is running or queued, avoiding
+overlapping diagnostics. Watch polls completed-window events every 0.5 seconds by
+default. "--json" exports JSON Lines and "--duration 30" limits a capture to 30 seconds.
+
+The native timing loops have no new per-sample logging. Existing exported reports
+retain errno, coverage, A/B medians, positive pair counts, half-window statistics and
+confirmation windows where the detector provides them. A detector finishes before
+its full results become available; retained startup results are labelled "snapshot"
+and do not invent a fresh duration.
+
+Direct ADB equivalents:
+
+~~~sh
+adb shell content read --uri content://com.eltavine.duckdetector.diagnostics/status
+adb shell content call --uri content://com.eltavine.duckdetector.diagnostics --method scan --arg selinux
+adb shell content read --uri content://com.eltavine.duckdetector.diagnostics/events?after=0
+adb shell content read --uri content://com.eltavine.duckdetector.diagnostics/report/selinux
+~~~
+
+## Transport and lifecycle
+
+The provider is protected by the platform DUMP permission and also explicitly accepts
+only the owning app UID, root UID 0, or ADB shell UID 2000 at every implemented entry
+point. Granting DUMP to another app is not enough. This explicit check also covers call
+and getType, whose framework permission rules differ from query/openFile.
+
+Each events response starts with a protocol 1 cursor record: process instance, newest
+and oldest sequence, attachment state, and gap/reset indicators. The journal retains
+128 events. Each event report preview is limited to 16,384 characters and explicitly
+marks truncation; the report endpoint retains complete latest results. Reconnecting
+clients must honor the cursor rather than assuming an uninterrupted history. Requests
+have IDs, and queued/running scans never expose the previous report as a fresh result.
+
+Provider reads return finite UTF-8 pipes, so an abandoned watcher does not leave a
+permanent stream thread. Scan work stays on the existing app session and preserves its
+normal process isolation, failure interpretation and scan serialization.
+
+Platform references (Android 16; the public APIs used here are available at minSdk 29):
+
+- [ContentProvider.call permission contract](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/ContentProvider#call(java.lang.String,java.lang.String,android.os.Bundle))
+- [AOSP ContentProvider transport](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/android-16.0.0_r1/core/java/android/content/ContentProvider.java)
+- [AOSP DUMP permission](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/android-16.0.0_r1/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml)
+- [AOSP shell content command](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/android-16.0.0_r1/cmds/content/src/com/android/commands/content/Content.java)
